NAME: Funding launch check
OWNER: Funding Launch
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every weekday (Monday to Friday) at 9:07 AM, until Dan marks the business launched
MILESTONE: 1
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Dan says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/spike-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Funding launch check" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", write "Funding launch check: not switched on" to this month's file in /workspace/spike-team/log/ and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Dan only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST".
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/spike-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/spike-team/context/owner.md is missing, write NO_CLIENT_SOURCE to the log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. If nothing changed, write "no change" and stop.
Run record: end every run with one line in this month's file in /workspace/spike-team/log/: the time, "Funding launch check", and done, no change, not switched on, blocked (why) or failed (why), with counts. If you stopped at the switch check or the isolation guard, the line you wrote there is this run's record; don't add a second.

Use the funding-launch-checklist skill. Read /workspace/spike-team/context/funding-launch.md, anything new in /workspace/spike-team/context/funding-project/, and anything new in GHL (read only). If you can't read the status board or the checklist, write "launch status unknown: <what you couldn't read>" instead of "no change". Write to /workspace/spike-team/daily/<today>/funding.md: done since yesterday, blocked and on whom, the next three steps only Dan can take, and whether Dan's launch date was met or how many days are left. If the checklist says launched, write "launched" and stop; Dan can then switch this routine off.
